 "drivingQuestion": "Are women prevented from sounding the shofar on a Festival?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "contradiction resolved as a tannaitic dispute; the underlying dispute is cited in the next unit",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "rosh_hashanah.33a.5",
   "daf": "33a",
   "sentenceId": 4,
   "he": "אֵין מְעַכְּבִין אֶת הַתִּינוֹקוֹת מִלִּתְקוֹעַ. הָא נָשִׁים — מְעַכְּבִין, וְהָתַנְיָא: אֵין מְעַכְּבִין לֹא אֶת הַנָּשִׁים וְלֹא אֶת הַתִּינוֹקוֹת מִלִּתְקוֹעַ בְּיוֹם טוֹב! אֲמַר אַבָּיֵי, לָא קַשְׁיָא: הָא רַבִּי יְהוּדָה, הָא רַבִּי יוֹסֵי וְרַבִּי שִׁמְעוֹן.",
   "en": "§ The mishna further teaches: «One» need «not prevent children from sounding» the shofar on Rosh HaShana. The Gemara infers: If «women» wish to sound the shofar, «one» indeed «prevents» them from doing so. The Gemara asks: «Isn’t it taught» in a baraita that «one does not prevent women or children from sounding» the shofar «on a Festival?» The Gemara answers that «Abaye said:» This is «not difficult: This» mishna is in accordance with the opinion of «Rabbi Yehuda,» while «that» baraita is in accordance with the opinion of «Rabbi Yosei and Rabbi Shimon.»"
  }
 ],
